//  PETPORTS -- RGB LAMP MODULE EFFECT
//
//  THE PLAIN LAMP EFFECT WITH A SCRIPT, AND THE SCRIPT IS THE ONLY DIFFERENCE.
//  petports_module_light is this file without `scripts`, because its colour is
//  baked into its animation and never moves.
//
//  animationConfig IS WHAT GRANTS THE SCRIPT ITS animator, AND THAT IS NOT
//  INCIDENTAL. A status effect only gains access to the animator table when
//  this property is non-nil -- so the light and the script that recolours it
//  have to arrive together, in this file, or the script has nothing to talk to.
//
//  APPLIED PERSISTENTLY AND NEVER BY DURATION. The port calls
//  status.setPersistentEffects, which holds an effect for as long as it is in
//  the set and drops it the moment it leaves. `defaultDuration` is unread on
//  that path; it is stated at vanilla's value so an effect applied some other
//  way later behaves like the augment this was copied from.
//
//  NO effectConfig. A colour cannot be carried here -- setPersistentEffects
//  takes effect names and no payload -- which is the entire reason the colour
//  travels as a status property and the script reads it. See the script.

{
	"name" : "petports_module_rgblight",

	"effectConfig" : {},

	"defaultDuration" : 5,

	"scripts" : [ "/stats/effects/lofty_petports/petports_module_rgblight.lua" ],
	"scriptDelta" : 5,

	"animationConfig" : "petports_module_rgblight.animation"
}
